				<h2 class="newsletter-article-title">Utah and Texas V2X Accelerator Sites Advance to Phase 2</h2>
				<div class="newsletter-article-content">
					<p>
						The V2X Accelerator sites led by the Utah Department of Transportation
						(UDOT) and Texas A&amp;M Transportation Institute (TTI) reached a
						major milestone in September 2026, wrapping up <strong>Phase 1: Finalize Design,
						Build and Test</strong>. Both sites completed all required
						testing and demonstrated that their systems operate safely and as
						designed. Now in <strong>Phase 2: Operate and Evaluate</strong>, UDOT and TTI will focus on
						demonstrating intersite interoperability, assessing operational
						performance and deployment impacts and benefits, and documenting a
						reference implementation for other deployers. The third V2X
						Accelerator site, led by the Maricopa County Department of
						Transportation, is on track to enter Phase 2 in early 2027.
					</p>
					<p>
						All Phase 1 V2X Accelerator reports will be posted
						<a href="https://www.its.dot.gov/research-areas/V2X-Deployment/deployment/accelerator/documentation/">here</a>
						as they become available.
					</p>
					<div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
						<a href="https://www.its.dot.gov/research-areas/V2X-Deployment/deployment/accelerator/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="newsletter-cta">
