			<article id="connected-vehicle-core-services-toolset-version-2-5-0" class="newsletter-article">
				<figure class="newsletter-image">
					<img
						src="https://content.govdelivery.com/attachments/fancy_images/USDOTFHWA/2026/10/14605470/cvcs-toolset-user-interface_original.png"
						alt="Connected Vehicle Core Services Toolset user interface"
					/>
					<figcaption>Source: USDOT</figcaption>
				</figure>
				<h2 class="newsletter-article-title">Connected Vehicle Core Services (CVCS) Toolset Version 2.5.0 Introduces New Features and Enhancements</h2>
				<div class="newsletter-article-content">
					<p>
						Version 2.5.0 of the CVCS Toolset introduces new features that make it
						easier to create, check, and troubleshoot the standardized digital
						messages that connected vehicles rely on to &ldquo;talk&rdquo; to roadside equipment.
						The open-source, web-based toolset includes three tools: the
						MAP/Road Geometry Attributes (RGA) Creator Tool, which creates
						digital representations of intersections and roadways, along with
						RGA messages describing broader roadway details; the Traveler Information
						Messages (TIM) Creator Tool, which builds TIMs that deliver roadway
						advisories to vehicles; and the Message Validator Tool, which reads
						an encoded message and displays its contents, helping users confirm
						it was built correctly. New features include the ability to upload
						custom imagery and align it with a live map, improved drawing and
						editing capabilities, automatic elevation calculations, support for
						additional lane types, and indicators for required data fields. The
						Message Validator Tool also supports additional message types,
						provides more readable results and detailed error explanations, and
						improves message transmission security, helping agencies produce
						more accurate and reliable connected vehicle messages with less
						effort. For more information about the CVCS Toolset, email
						<a href="mailto:CAVSupportServices@dot.gov">CAVSupportServices@dot.gov</a>.
					</p>
					<div class="newsletter-cta-wrapper align-right">
						<a href="https://github.com/usdot-fhwa-stol/connectedvcs-tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="newsletter-cta">
							<strong>See What's New in Version 2.5.0</strong>
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</article>
